description:
Context: CHROTE serves two response shapes. tmux handlers and the health endpoint return FLAT JSON via core.WriteJSON (e.g. {success, session, timestamp}); beads/services use core.WriteSuccess which wraps payloads in {success, data, timestamp}. The dashboard reads the flat fields directly (response.session, response.killed, health.bdVersion). chrt-idhj.6 and chrt-idhj.7 must NOT standardize the flat shapes, because wrapping them silently breaks every existing reader. This bead writes characterization (golden) tests that lock the current wire contract so any accidental envelope change fails loudly. It is the safety net that makes the .6/.7 refactor safe; write it before that work.

Current behavior to pin:
- POST /api/tmux/sessions -> {success, session, timestamp}
- DELETE /api/tmux/sessions/{name} -> {success, killed, timestamp}
- DELETE /api/tmux/sessions/all -> {success, killed, sessions, protected, timestamp}
- PATCH /api/tmux/sessions/{name} -> {success, oldName, newName, timestamp}
- GET /api/tmux/sessions/{name}/capture -> {content, session}
- POST /api/tmux/appearance -> {success, applied, total, timestamp}
- /api/beads/health and /api/health current shapes.

Desired: a Go httptest test per endpoint asserts the exact top-level keys, asserts NO 'data' wrapper on flat endpoints and presence of the envelope on enveloped ones, with volatile fields (timestamp) normalized; tests fail if a flat shape is wrapped or an enveloped one unwrapped.

Scope: in scope = table-driven response-shape tests under src/internal/api plus a short documented list of which endpoints are intentionally flat. Out of scope = changing any handler or response shape (tests only) and any frontend change.

Safety: tests only; no runtime change; do not restart chrote.service.

## Required Skills
beads-workflow,test-driven-development,verification-before-completion
